
- A는 B이자 C이다
    - A has been both [B] and [C]
        > Competence has been both my identity and my limitation

- 더 이상 A가 아니라 B로 전락하다
    - A is no longer [B]; instead, it turns into [C]
        > Reality is no longer solid ground; instead, it turns into a mire
- A가 아니라 B를 ~하는 곳
    - not a place to [A], but a place where [B]
        > Not a place where we belong, but a place where we feel we shouldn't exist
- ~가 …하는 것을 단념시키다, 말리다, 못하게 막다 (의욕을 꺾다)
    > The fear of failure discouraged him from taking action
- 돌아오는 길에, 돌아가는 도중에
    - on the way back
        > talked with him on the way back home
